Do not know DMP and LVM alt links, but if you mean multipathing to
disk devices, this is done at device driver level in TRU64 v5. And
then, it is offered to the upper level : advfs, ufs, raw devices, and
LSM :-) ... This multipath does load balancing and automatic failover
:

If you use FC, dual FC HBA to a switch, even accessing a single unit,
you will see load balancing and failover over your two cables. I
recently made some measurements on file system access to ONE disk,
reaching 160 Mb/s on a 1 Gbs FC which is 100 Mb/s max per cable.

If a path is failing, rollback on IO is done and IO is rescheduled to
a valid path.

You can see all (valid) paths to disk using :

hwmgr -show scsi -full 


Emmanuel


