In article <8940abed.0201250632.425b2fc@posting.google.com>, hoshisato@hotmail.com (Hoshisato) writes:

>Hello,
>From a program on a Tru64 system I need to forward the the CPU, DISK,
>IO and PAGINGINFO statistics to another node. On HP Unix I used
>pstat.h and sysinfo.h, but those interfaces don't seem to exist on
>Tru64. What interfaces do I need to use?

A lot of performance data is available using the table(2) system
call, with some available through getsysinfo(2).  For other bits
you may have use the undoucmented Mach interface or go reading
kernel memory directly.  For those cases you're best off finding
the source of one of the free performance monitoring programs and
see how they get the information.  Monitor is one such program:

ftp.digital.com:/pub/DEC/monitor.alpha.tar.Z

The manual pages for table(2) and getsysinfo(2) may not document
all the available data structures, so go looking through the
include files.  Newer versions often support getting more data
than older versions.
