>to be ok, and as far as I can tell, everything is where it should be...

This is often a problem with /dev entries. Boot to single user
and see if /dev/console is there:

# ls -l /dev/console
crw--w--w-   1 root     terminal   0,  0 Jan 25 10:17 /dev/console

If not, mount / read-write (# mount -u /), then cd to /dev and do:

# MAKEDEV console

There could be other things in the path that are busted, like gettydefs
or getty itself, or ......

