> "MAKEDEV: not found "

cd /dev
./MAKEDEV console
if well configured, which is the case, '.' is not in root path.

this comes from /etc/inittab which runs all getty (login prompt) to
serial devices. Looking at your message, console can be the culprit.

check :
ls -al /dev/console
crw--w--w-   1 root     terminal   0,  0 Jan 29 11:07 /dev/console
ls -al /dev/tty0[0-1] if you have a serial console
ls -al /dev/tty0[0-1]
crw-rw-rw-   1 root     system    35,  0 Dec 20  2000 /dev/tty00
crw-rw-rw-   1 root     system    35,  1 Aug 28 17:50 /dev/tty01

grep getty /etc/inittab
cons:1234:respawn:/usr/sbin/getty console console vt100 

respawn in the 3rd field, asks init process to respawn indefinitely
the getty command each time getty vanishes. getty is failing, so there
is a bad loop in here.

You'll see that behavior if you declare lat devices and you boot a
kernel with no lat subsystem as well.

