Hi Peter,
> 
> Does anyone know if it would be possible to triple boot linux, VMS,
> Tru64 off of SRM on the same system?

Sure it is - just install every OS on another Harddisk.
You only have to pay attention to the bootflags.
Always boot OpenVMS with the -fl 0 qualifier and Tru64 with the -fl a
qualifier.
I never tried Linux (don't need a crap Unix if I have Tru64), so I don't
know the bootflags for this one.

> Also would it be possible to have the three OS residing off of one hard
> disk.

No, that won't work.
You need a seperate HDD for every OS you have.
Although it is possible to have multiple copies of OpenVMS (different
Versions) on one HDD.

Greetings - Freddy


