Once upon a time, Patrick Young <P.Young@unsw.EDU.AU> said:
>I would expect you could put Tru64 and Linux on the same disk as Linux
>can work with BSD disklabels. As an interesting exercise you might want
>to see if there is a way to mount Tru64 partitions under Linux.

If you use UFS under Tru64, you should be able to read (haven't tried
write, but I think it should work) those partitions from Linux.  You
can't access AdvFS domains from Linux (that's a proprietary filesystem).
AFAIK, Tru64 has no support for reading anything that you can write
under Linux (except for CD-ROMs).
