I joined the DECUS, U.S. Chapter well over 20 years ago to stay
abreast of the developments (and frankly to have an "in" on getting
patches) for my PDP-11/RSX-11D system. I switched from being a passive
member to an active volunteer about 15 years ago. By then, my
interests had expanded to learning how to squeeze the last processing
cycles out of a memory constrained VAX 750 that was supporting over 20
developers. From kilobytes of memory and single digit megahertz of
processor cycle time (remember when 1 VAX Unit of  Processing was
standard?) to today's gigabytes and gigahertz, the world of
technology, and perhaps most importantly, those of us who rely upon it
have evolved dramatically. 

My user group involvement has grown over the years culminating into my
current position as president. What I know for sure is that the
dedication of elected directors, board members and countless
volunteers  has paved the way for our many accomplishments this past
year. I extend my heartfelt thanks to these and all of you for your
participation, which has had added untold value to our membership. 

The start of each New Year brings newcomers, newly elected leaders
(see ENCOMPASS ELECTS FOUR DIRECTORS article below), and the
opportunity for new resolutions to do more and be better. This year I
resolve to focus my energy towards the continued viability of our
39-year old user group and to provide each of you with the tools
necessary to best leverage your current technologies and to best
prepare for what's to come. 

I likewise invite each of you to resolve to renew your membership
https://safe2.sba.com/encompass/memberApp/individual.cfm, to be more
involved, and stay connected with your peers. 

As you hopefully already know, Encompass is making a major push this
year to revitalize our Membership Program. We are putting some serious
teeth into the tangible benefits such as the just announced _Shannon
Knows Compaq_ subscription savings in addition to the numerous, but
more intangible benefits of meeting and sharing your experiences with
your peers, the experts in the field, and those who provide the
products and services you use. There are some significant cost
incentives to consider renewing your 
membership early this year. For more information on our membership
program and the incentives currently running, look for the article
MEMBERSHIP RENEWAL DISCOUNT EXTENDED article below. 

For me, Encompass is a community of peers who do more than share
experiences "from the trenches." We are mentors. We are prot�g�s. We
are invested in each other's success. And because of it, we will do
more than succeed. We will triumph. 

Joe Pollizzi 
