Overview
64 MB to 1.5 GB synchronous DRAM main memory.

Size
32MB Memory
64MB Memory
128MB Memory
256MB Memory


Configuration

    a.. There are three memory banks (J1/J2, J3/J4, and J5/J6) in the
system; each bank consists of two DIMMs.
    b.. Two DIMMs are required because the memory bus width is 144-bits (128
bits of data and 16 bits of ECC).
    c.. Each DIMM in a bank supplies 72 bits of the 144-bit bus width.
    d.. Both DIMMs in a bank must be identical, and both must be populated.
    e.. DIMM sets do not have to be identical
    f.. Memory banks can be populated in any order. The POST code
automatically maps the largest banks to the lowest addresses starting at
00.0000.0000, which prevents holes in the memory address space.
    g.. DIMMs available so far allow only up to 768 MBytes
To ensure a match, the POST code use the I2C bus to read each DIMM's
characteristics from a ROM on the DIMM. If identical pairs are not
installed, thecode may reject the DIMMs and flag the memory as unavailable.







