hum, seems to be -1- routing problem, -2- or firewall/proxy settings
in between, -3- some security setting on the unix side.

My best bet is -1-, so :

As a first test, try :

from you client computer :
if unix " traceroute xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx" (@ of compaq computer)
if windows " tracert xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx" in a cmd 

You'll see the routing path used to try to access the destination.

then 'traceroute' from your intermediate unix system, where you'll
find a valid route.

Finally add a route on your client side ( man route on Unix or route
/? on Windows cmd).

Should do the trick

Cheers


