PC business, which logged revenue of $3.8 billion and an operating
loss of $69 million.

Compaq has been struggling in the PC market amid dwindling demand and
increased pricing pressure. The company has taken a number of steps
over the past year to improve profits there, including laying off
workers, outsourcing the production of its portable computers and
working off inventories.

