So I installed a working Yamaha 6416 SCSI CDRW into my AlphaStation 250
4/266.  Prior to installation, I jumpered the 512 byte block size jumper
because the manual and another newsgroup posting suggested to.  After
installation, both Tru64 and Alpha Linux could read the disk, however,
when I tested the "boot" process with bootable Tru64 5.1A and Redhat 7.1
CD's, early in the boot process I got a perplexing message:

   "...not 512 byte block size device..."

But, both Tru64 and AlphaLinux finished their boot processes....

So, I took the jumper off.  Both Tru64 and Alpha Linux can still boot
but WITHOUT the "...not a 512 byte block device..." message.

As it is now (without jumper), both OS's can read and write to the disk
without the jumper.

Should I be worried?  How do others configure their CD-RW's?

-bb



