In article <58ba0101.0201040632.42762b6@posting.google.com>,
Andrew Rycroft <andrew.rycroft@intrinsitech.com> wrote:
> I recently tried to read the mail messages on my Tru64UNIX system with
> the mail utility.

Which one? Tru64 comes with four mail programs:

	mail	The traditional UNIX mail program, 30 years old now, and
		clumsy.

	Mail	Berkeley mail (sometimes called mailx)

	MH	The Mail Handler system. This doesn't run as a separate mail
		program, but uses commands like "scan" and "show" at the
		shell level.

	dxmail	A graphical X-Window mail program that provides a mouse/window
		based front end to MH.

You're probably trying to use the old UNIX mail. It's pretty horrible. Try
the "Mail" or "dxmail" commands instead.

