Itamar Caspi wrote:

> Our Alfa system works in RT with root permission.
> We've encountered a priority inversion problem between our processes.
> 
> I know how to solve this by boosting priorities before locking the
> shared memory.
> I also know that Solaris solves this problem in OS level using mutexes
> and priority inheretance (pthread_mutexattr_setprotocol with
> THREAD_PRIO_PROTECT).
> 
> My question is: Does Digital Unix have a solution similar to Solaris,
> as described above ?

We don't currently implement priority inheritance. It's extraordinarily 
complicated to do it right, because threads may own multiple mutexes, and 
all the dependency graph needs to be dealt with when adjusting priorities. 
It's a "big deal", and we've had too little demand and too many other "big 
deals" that were easier.

If it's ever done, though, I can assure you it will never appear on 
"version 4.0" (or even 4.0G). It'll be something beyond 5.1A and might 
possibly show up later as a patch for 5.1 and 5.1A.

