beyond maintenance-level activity.  So I don't feel there's much to lose by
trying to shake things up, and damn good reason to do so (not only to
increase VMS's future potential, but to let corporations know that there are
*some* things customers simply won't take lying down, and thus have a
salutary effect on future decisions).  Other viewpoints may differ.

